assive, sentient robot which has a clear parallel in Laputa's automaton guardians.","direction":"outgoing"},{"source":"aw186","target":"aw191","type":"inspired_by","label":"Inspired By","note":"As his first feature film, it established Miyazaki's signature style of dynamic chase sequences, European-inspired settings, and morally ambiguous 'rogue' characters, all of which were refined and expanded upon in 'Castle in the Sky'.","direction":"outgoing"},{"source":"aw186","target":"aw189","type":"inspired_by","label":"Inspired By","note":"Miyazaki's directorial work on this TV series served as a template for many themes in 'Castle in the Sky', including a post-apocalyptic setting, a plucky boy protagonist with incredible physical abilities, a mysterious girl with a connection to a powerful force, and the critique of technology.","direction":"outgoing"},{"source":"aw186","target":"aw190","type":"inspired_by","label":"Inspired By","note":"Miyazaki expressed admiration for the Fleischer Superman cartoons, and critics note a likely influence in the design of Laputa's giant robots and the dynamic sense of scale and destruction.","direction":"outgoing"}],"lineage":{"influenced_by":["aw186","aw186","aw186","aw186","aw186","aw186","aw186"],"influences":[]},"stats":{"total_connected":7,"influences_count":4,"influenced_count":3,"filter":"all","vault_count":0,"beyond_count":7}}